sture specification on raw materials, jacket leak testing, high temperature trip"},{"node":"Solids charging and dryer","deviation":"Dust cloud","cause":"Open charging of powder, dryer discharge","consequence":"Combustible dust explosion (aspirin and salicylic acid dusts)","safeguard":"Closed charging with nitrogen inerting, earthing and bonding, explosion venting, dust extraction"},{"node":"Acetic anhydride storage and transfer","deviation":"Loss of containment","cause":"Hose or gasket failure","consequence":"Corrosive and toxic vapour release, flammable liquid pool","safeguard":"Bunding, dry break couplings, vapour detection, PPE and safety showers"},{"node":"Mother liquor still","deviation":"Air ingress under vacuum","cause":"Seal or flange leak","consequence":"Flammable acetic acid and anhydride vapour mixture in the column and vacuum system","safeguard":"Nitrogen bleed, oxygen monitoring on the vacuum line, flame arrester on the vent"}],"process_hazards":[{"hazard":"Flammable materials","detail":"Acetic anhydride, Acetic acid. Hazardous area classification, ignition source control, gas detection, fire protection."},{"hazard":"Toxic materials","detail":"Acetic anhydride. Toxic gas detection, emergency shutdown and isolation, escape sets, minimise inventory."},{"hazard":"Corrosive materials","detail":"Acetic anhydride, Acetic acid. Material selection, PPE, safety showers, bunded storage."}],"validation":[{"metric":"Overall aspirin yield on salicylic acid, crystallisation route","model":95.646673,"published":[91.0,97.4],"unit":"% of theoretical","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"US 3,235,583 (prior art crystallisation route, 91%) and US 3,373,187 (catalysed batch, 97.4%)","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US3235583A/en","note":"Model yield comes from the conversion, first crop, second crop and handling losses, not set directly.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":3,"pass":true},{"metric":"Acetic acid by-product recovered","model":94.723691,"published":97.0,"unit":"% of acetic acid made","error_pct":-2.34671,"inside_range":null,"source":"US 3,235,583","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US3235583A/en","note":"Patent: recovery of by-product acetic acid in the neighbourhood of 97%. Model figure is net of the diluent lost with the residue purge.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":5,"pass":true},{"metric":"Reaction temperature","model":85.0,"published":[40.0,90.0],"unit":"C","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"Ullmann's Encyclopedia of Industrial Chemistry via PubChem HSDB (below 90 C); US 3,235,583 claims 40 to 95 C","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug_view/data/compound/2244/JSON?heading=Methods+of+Manufacturing","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":0,"pass":true},{"metric":"Production cost against the market price of aspirin","model":6991.766533,"published":[2356,2887],"unit":"USD/t","error_pct":142.181037,"inside_range":false,"source":"IMARC Group, Aspirin Pricing Report, Q4 2025 (Germany 2,356 to USA 2,887 USD/t)","url":"https://www.imarcgroup.com/aspirin-pricing-report","note":"Shown for information. A 10 t/d plant carries a heavy labour and capital charge per tonne compared with the large Chinese producers that set the bulk price.","kind":"cost","tolerance_pct":null,"pass":null}],"assumptions":["Batch operation is shown as time averaged flows over 8,000 h a year.","Reaction completion 97% after 2 h at 85 C without catalyst, and 68% of the aspirin formed crystallising on cooling, both from US 3,373,187 Table I (run 3).","90% of the aspirin left in the mother liquor is won back as a second crop from the still residue (assumed; US 3,235,583 describes the filtrate being distilled for more product).","Acetic acid and anhydride recovered overhead in the still: 97% (US 3,235,583).","Wet cake holds 10 wt% mother liquor; the salicylic acid it carries ends up in the dried product as a trace. Pharmacopoeia grade may need a recrystallisation, not modelled.","Dryer dust and packing losses 0.5% of the aspirin dried.","Reaction enthalpy from solid aspirin and salicylic acid and liquid anhydride and acid standard heats of formation; heats of solution and crystallisation are not included.","Hydrolysis of anhydride by moisture and by-products such as acetylsalicylic anhydride and salsalate are not modelled; they end up in the residue purge in practice.","The residue purge goes to incineration and is charged at the default effluent rate, which understates the true incineration cost.","Crystalliser cooling below 30 C needs chilled water; it is costed as cooling water.","A packing line allowance of 0.75 M USD (GMP finishing) is added as a lump; this is an estimate, not a quote."],"notes":[]}